EXAM_DATA.papers["2020-english-one"] = {"id":"2020-english-one","year":2020,"label":"2020 英语一","era":"modern","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2020-english-one/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"estimated","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Even if families don't sit down to eat together as frequently as before, millions of Britons will nonetheless have got a share this weekend of one of that nation's great traditions: the Sunday roast.   {{1}}   a cold winter's day, few culinary pleasures can   {{2}}   it. Yet as we report now, the food police are determined that this   {{3}}   should be rendered yet another guilty pleasure   {{4}}   to damage our health."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"The Food Standards Authority (FSA) has   {{5}}   a public warning about the risks of a compound called acrylamide that forms in some foods cooked   {{6}}   high temperatures. This means that people should   {{7}}   crisping their roast potatoes, reject thin-crust pizzas and only   {{8}}   toast their bread. But where is the evidence to support such alarmist advice?   {{9}}   studies have shown that acrylamide can cause neurological damage in mice, there is no   {{10}}   evidence that it causes cancer in humans."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"Scientists say the compound is   {{11}}   to cause cancer but have no hard scientific proof.   {{12}}   the precautionary principle, it could be argued that it is   {{13}}   to follow the FSA advice.   {{14}}   , it was rumoured that smoking caused cancer for years before the evidence was found to prove a   {{15}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"Doubtless a piece of boiled beef can always be   {{16}}   up on Sunday alongside some steamed vegetables, without the Yorkshire pudding and no wine. But would life be worth living?   {{17}}   , the FSA says it is not telling people to cut out roast foods   {{18}}   , but to reduce their lifetime intake. However, their   {{19}}   risks coming across as being pushy and overprotective. Constant health scares just   {{20}}   with no one listening."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In"},{"key":"B","text":"On"},{"key":"C","text":"Till"},{"key":"D","text":"Towards"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"1.","reason":"具体某一天前用 on 线索就在本句内 __(1)__ a cold winter's day。a cold winter's day 是'某个具体的日子'，英语里'在某天'恒用介词 on（on a cold day / on that morning），这条搭配规则直接指向答案。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"In 用于较大时间段（in winter、in the morning），不与'a cold winter's day'这种具体某天搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"On 正是表示'在某个具体日子'的介词，与 a cold winter's day 完全契合，自然引出'在寒冷冬日里没什么美食能比得上它'。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Till 意为'直到某时为止'，放进'__一个寒冷冬日'里语义不通，也不与'某天'构成地点/时点框架。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Towards 表'朝向/接近'，towards evening 可指'傍晚时分'，但与'a cold winter's day'搭配不当、语义也不对。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"match"},{"key":"B","text":"express"},{"key":"C","text":"satisfy"},{"key":"D","text":"influence"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"few + can，表'几乎没有别的能比得上' 线索是本句的否定主语结构 few culinary pleasures can __(2)__ it。few（几乎没有）+ 后文盛赞，说明作者要表达'几乎没有别的美食能与之相比/匹敌'，答案应是'比得上、匹敌'之义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"match 意为'与……相匹敌、比得上'，'few pleasures can match it'即'几乎没有别的乐趣能比得上它'，是对烤肉的最高赞美，与 few culinary pleasures 完美契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"express 意为'表达'，'乐趣表达它'语义不通，乐趣不是表达的施动者。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"satisfy 是'满足'，通常是食物满足人，而非'其他乐趣满足烤肉（it）'，主宾关系颠倒，且偏离'比得上'之义。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"influence 表'影响'，'乐趣影响它'与上下文'盛赞烤肉无可比拟'毫不相干。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"patience"},{"key":"B","text":"concern"},{"key":"C","text":"surprise"},{"key":"D","text":"enjoyment"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"this 回指'美食之乐'，后文又称 guilty pleasure 线索跨句：前句盛赞 few culinary pleasures can __(2)__ it，本句又把它叫作 another guilty pleasure。pleasure（乐趣/享受）两头呼应，说明空填的名词应等于'享受'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"patience'耐心'与'吃烤肉的享受'毫无指代关系。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"concern'担忧、关切'是负面/中性词，而此处指代的是正面的'享受'，与后文 guilty pleasure 中的 pleasure 对不上。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"surprise'惊讶'未在前文出现，无法回指被赞美的'美食之乐'。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"enjoyment'享受、乐趣'正好回指前文 culinary pleasures，并与后文 guilty pleasure 的 pleasure 同义复现，'这一享受要被打成又一项有罪的快感'逻辑顺畅。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"intensified"},{"key":"B","text":"guaranteed"},{"key":"C","text":"compelled"},{"key":"D","text":"privileged"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"讽刺语气：被'认定'必然损害健康 线索是全句反讽基调 this __(3)__ should be rendered yet another guilty pleasure __(4)__ to damage our health。作者借'食物警察'之口，把烤肉说成'被保证/认定会损害健康'，需一个能接 to do 且表'被断定（会怎样）'的词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"intensified'被加强'不与 to do 搭配，'享受被加强去损害健康'也讲不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"guaranteed 有固定用法 be guaranteed to do（必定会、保证会），'这一享受被打成又一项保准会损害健康的有罪快感'，既搭配正确，又精准传达作者对该警告的反讽。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"compelled'强迫'通常 compel sb to do，主语应是人或可被迫者，'乐趣被强迫去损害健康'对象错位。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"privileged'享有特权的'是褒义，与'损害健康'的负面语境冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ignored"},{"key":"B","text":"received"},{"key":"C","text":"issued"},{"key":"D","text":"cancelled"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"下文全是 FSA 在劝告公众，说明它'发出'了警告 线索在后文：FSA 主张 people should __(7)__ crisping their roast potatoes 等一系列建议，可见 FSA 是警告的发出方，不是接收方或取消方，答案应为'发布/发出'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"ignored'无视'与下文 FSA 大力劝告公众的行为自相矛盾。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"received'收到'把 FSA 当成接收方，但全文 FSA 是警告的发布者、劝告者，方向相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"issued 与 a public warning 构成固定搭配 issue a warning（发布警告），主语 FSA 作为权威机构发布公众警告，与后文它给出的种种劝告完全一致。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"cancelled'取消'意味警告不再生效，但下文 FSA 仍在执行该警告、劝人少吃，逻辑冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"under"},{"key":"B","text":"by"},{"key":"C","text":"for"},{"key":"D","text":"at"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"at + 温度，表'在某温度下' 线索就在本句 cooked __(6)__ high temperatures。英语表示'在某温度/速度/价位'恒用 at（at high temperatures、at high speed），这条搭配直接给出答案。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"under 多表'在……之下/在……条件下'（under pressure），不与具体温度构成'在某温度下烹饪'的标准搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"by 表方式或增减幅度，'by high temperatures'不能表达'在高温下'。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"for 常表持续时间或目的，与温度搭配不当。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"at 与温度搭配最地道，at high temperatures（在高温下）是标准说法，'在高温下烹制的某些食物'语义通顺。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"forget"},{"key":"B","text":"avoid"},{"key":"C","text":"finish"},{"key":"D","text":"regret"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"7.","reason":"并列 reject、only partially，全是'少做/别做' 线索在并列结构 reject thin-crust pizzas and only __(8)__ toast their bread。同句的 reject（拒绝）、only…toast（只稍微烤）都是'减少、避免'的方向，空填的动词也应与之同向，表'避免'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"forget + doing 指'忘记曾做过某事'，与'劝人别把土豆烤脆'的告诫不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"avoid + doing 即'避免做某事'，'人们应避免把烤土豆做得焦脆'，与并列的 reject thin-crust pizzas 同为'少做/别做'，契合 FSA 的健康告诫。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"finish'完成'是鼓励做，与劝人减少高温烹饪的语境方向相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"regret + doing'后悔做过'描述事后情绪，不是劝人当下别做的告诫。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"easily"},{"key":"B","text":"regularly"},{"key":"C","text":"partially"},{"key":"D","text":"initially"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"only + 减害基调，要'只稍微烤' 线索是 only 与全句减害方向 only __(8)__ toast their bread。前文都在劝'少烤、别烤焦'，only 强调'仅仅、有限度地'，故应是'只把面包烤到部分程度'，即'稍微烤一下'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"easily'容易地'不涉及'烤的程度多少'，不合 only 的限度含义。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"regularly'经常'是鼓励多做，与劝人减少高温烤制的语境相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"partially'部分地、不完全地'与 only 呼应，'只把面包烤到部分程度（即别烤焦）'，正是减少 acrylamide 的告诫，与前文'避免烤脆'同向。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"initially'最初、起初'是时间副词，与'烤的程度'无关。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"If"},{"key":"B","text":"Since"},{"key":"C","text":"While"},{"key":"D","text":"Unless"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"9.","reason":"前句'对老鼠有害'、后句'对人无致癌证据'，是对比让步 线索是前后两分句的对照：前半 studies have shown that acrylamide can cause neurological damage in mice（动物身上有害），后半 there is no __(10)__ evidence that it causes cancer in humans（人身上无确凿致癌证据）。一'有'一'无'形成转折/让步，需 While（尽管/虽然）这类对比连词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"If'如果'表假设条件，但前句是已被研究证实的事实（studies have shown），不是假设，逻辑不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Since'既然/因为'表因果，但'对老鼠有害'并不能推出'对人无致癌证据'，二者非因果而是对比。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"While'尽管、虽然'引导让步，'尽管研究显示它会损害老鼠神经，但并无确凿证据表明它致人患癌'，前后一正一反对照鲜明，与作者'质疑证据不足'的立场一致。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Unless'除非'引否定条件，'除非研究显示对老鼠有害'放进句中讲不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"conclusive"},{"key":"B","text":"external"},{"key":"C","text":"secondary"},{"key":"D","text":"negative"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"下文'无确凿科学证明'同义复现 线索在跨段呼应：第3段 have no hard scientific proof（没有确凿科学证明）与本空 no ___ evidence 是同义复现，说明作者强调缺的是'确凿、定论性的'证据，答案应为'结论性/确凿的'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"conclusive'确凿的、决定性的'，'没有确凿证据表明它致人患癌'正是作者反驳 alarmist advice 的核心，与下文 no hard scientific proof 同义复现。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"external'外部的'与'证据是否确凿'无关，不切作者论点。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"secondary'次要的'强调主次，作者要强调的是'缺乏确凿证据'，而非'缺乏次要证据'。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"negative'否定的/阴性的'，'没有否定证据'反而说明有正面证据，与作者立场相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"likely"},{"key":"B","text":"bound"},{"key":"C","text":"insufficient"},{"key":"D","text":"slow"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"11.","reason":"but no hard proof，说明只是'有可能' 线索在本句转折 the compound is __(11)__ to cause cancer but have no hard scientific proof。but 后'没有确凿证明'，说明前半只能是'可能、有几率'的弱断言，不能是'必定'，答案应为'likely（很可能）'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"likely 接 to do 表'很可能'，'该化合物很可能致癌，但没有确凿科学证明'——'可能'与'无定论'语气相称，正合作者'尚无定论'的论证。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"bound'必定、一定'语气太绝对，与后文 no hard scientific proof（没有确凿证明）矛盾——既无证明就不能说'必定'。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"insufficient'不足的'不与 to cause cancer 构成'不足以致癌'的合理表语，且语义偏离'科学家说它可能致癌'。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"slow'缓慢的'，'化合物缓慢致癌'与'有可能/无定论'的论点无关。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In addition to"},{"key":"B","text":"At the cost of"},{"key":"C","text":"On the basis of"},{"key":"D","text":"In contrast to"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"12.","reason":"凭原则得出'宜遵循建议'，是'依据'关系 线索是主从逻辑 __(12)__ the precautionary principle, it could be argued that it is __(13)__ to follow the FSA advice。后半'可以论证说遵循 FSA 建议是明智的'，正是'以预防原则为依据'推出的结论，故空填'on the basis of（基于、根据）'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"In addition to'除……之外（还）'表补充，但前文并无另一条与预防原则并列的依据可'补充'，逻辑不成立。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"At the cost of'以……为代价'，此处并非牺牲预防原则去换取什么，语义不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"On the basis of'基于、根据'，'基于预防原则，可以论证遵循 FSA 建议是明智的'，原则正是论证的依据，逻辑通顺，引出第3段的让步性讨论。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"In contrast to'与……形成对比'，但后句是顺着预防原则推论、并非与之相反，逻辑反了。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"interesting"},{"key":"B","text":"fortunate"},{"key":"C","text":"urgent"},{"key":"D","text":"advisable"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"基于预防原则，遵循建议是'明智可取的' 线索是前半的依据 __(12)__ the precautionary principle。预防原则主张'宁可谨慎'，由此推论'遵循 FSA 建议是值得/明智的'，答案应为'advisable（明智的、可取的）'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"interesting'有趣的'与'是否该遵循健康建议'这一明智与否的评价不在一个维度。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"fortunate'幸运的'，'遵循建议是幸运的'语义不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"urgent'紧急的'程度过强，与作者下文质疑该建议过度的态度不符；预防原则推出的是'谨慎可取'，并非'刻不容缓'。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"advisable'明智的、可取的'与 __(12)__ the precautionary principle 顺承——'基于预防原则，遵循 FSA 建议是明智的'，逻辑与程度都恰当。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"As usual"},{"key":"B","text":"After all"},{"key":"C","text":"By definition"},{"key":"D","text":"In particular"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"14.","reason":"吸烟致癌'先有传言后有证据'，为前句论点提供佐证 线索是前后两句关系：前句说'基于预防原则，谨慎遵循建议是明智的'；后句 it was rumoured that smoking caused cancer for years before the evidence was found 举吸烟的先例来支持'宁可先信'的道理，是补充说明理由，故用 After all（毕竟）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"As usual'像往常一样'暗示某事惯常发生，但此处是举一个历史先例佐证，不是说'惯例如此'。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"After all'毕竟'引出支持前句论断的理由——'毕竟吸烟致癌也是先有传言、多年后才找到证据'，为'宁可谨慎遵循建议'提供佐证，逻辑顺承。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"By definition'按定义来说'用于由概念本身推出结论，此处是举先例，不涉及定义。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"In particular'尤其、特别是'用于从一般到具体的强调，但前句并非泛述、后句也非其中某一项，逻辑不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"connection"},{"key":"B","text":"combination"},{"key":"C","text":"resemblance"},{"key":"D","text":"pattern"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"前文 smoking caused cancer，要证'两者有关联' 线索在同句前半 it was rumoured that smoking caused cancer。要找的证据是证明'吸烟与癌之间存在关联（因果联系）'，故空填'connection（联系、关联）'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"connection'联系、关联'正指'吸烟与癌之间的关联'，'证据被找到以证明（两者的）关联'，与前文 smoking caused cancer 的因果陈述对应。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"combination'组合、结合'指多物合在一起，不指'吸烟致癌'这种因果关联。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"resemblance'相似之处'指事物相像，吸烟与癌之间是因果而非相似关系。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"pattern'模式、规律'指反复出现的规律，不能精准表达'吸烟与癌之间的因果关联'。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"made"},{"key":"B","text":"used"},{"key":"C","text":"saved"},{"key":"D","text":"served"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"16.","reason":"宾语是食物、地点是 on Sunday 餐桌情境 线索在本句 a piece of boiled beef can always be __(16)__ up on Sunday alongside some steamed vegetables——周日把'水煮牛肉配蒸蔬菜'端上桌，serve up（上菜、端上）正合此饮食语境。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"made up 常表'编造、化妆、组成'，不表'把饭菜端上桌'。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"used up'用完、耗尽'，'把牛肉用尽'与'周日端上桌享用'语义不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"saved up 多表'攒钱、储蓄'，与'端菜上桌'无关。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"served up'端上、供应（饭菜）'，'周日总能端上一块水煮牛肉配蒸蔬菜'，与饮食情境完全契合，承接全文对'吃什么'的讨论。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To be brief"},{"key":"B","text":"For instance"},{"key":"C","text":"To be fair"},{"key":"D","text":"In general"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"17.","reason":"前文一直批 FSA，此处替它说句公道话 线索是态度转折：作者前文都在嘲讽 FSA 过度，本句却转述 the FSA says it is not telling people to cut out roast foods __(18)__, but to reduce their lifetime intake——替对方澄清'它并非叫人完全戒掉，只是减少摄入'，这是'公平地说'，故用 To be fair（平心而论）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"To be brief'简而言之'用于概括收束，但此处不是总结前文，而是替 FSA 说句公道话。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"For instance'例如'引出例证，但后句是转述 FSA 的整体立场、不是举某个例子。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"To be fair'平心而论、公平地说'，作者在通篇批评后退一步替 FSA 澄清'它并非要人完全戒掉，而是减少终身摄入'，态度转折自然，体现议论文的平衡笔法。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"In general'总的来说'用于概述普遍情况，此处是针对 FSA 立场给一句公道，不是泛述。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"entirely"},{"key":"B","text":"gradually"},{"key":"C","text":"reluctantly"},{"key":"D","text":"carefully"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"not cut out ___ but reduce，对照'完全戒'与'减少' 线索是 not...but 对照 not telling people to cut out roast foods __(18)__, but to reduce their lifetime intake。后半是'减少摄入'，前半'cut out（戒掉）'要与之对照，应是'完全戒掉'，故填 entirely（完全地）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"entirely'完全地'，'并非叫人完全戒掉烤食，而只是减少终身摄入'——'完全戒'与'只是减少'对照鲜明，正是 FSA 想澄清的分寸。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"gradually'逐渐地'与后半'减少'方向相近而非对照，无法凸显'完全戒'与'只减少'的反差。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"reluctantly'不情愿地'描述态度，不能与'减少'形成'完全 vs 部分'的程度对照。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"carefully'仔细地'修饰方式，与后半'减少摄入'不构成对照关系。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"promise"},{"key":"B","text":"competition"},{"key":"C","text":"experience"},{"key":"D","text":"campaign"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"19.","reason":"FSA 发警告、反复劝告，即一场宣传运动 线索跨段回指 FSA 的行为链：has __(5)__ a public warning、反复劝人少吃，再到末句 Constant health scares（持续不断的健康恐吓）。这一整套'反复发警告劝导公众'正是一场 campaign（运动、宣传活动），故选 campaign。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"promise'承诺'，FSA 做的是发警告、劝告，并未'承诺'什么，回指不上。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"competition'竞争'与 FSA 的行为毫无关联。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"experience'经验、经历'不能概括 FSA'反复发警告劝导公众'这一行动。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"campaign'（宣传）运动'正概括 FSA 持续发警告、劝公众减少高温食物的整套行动，'他们这场运动有显得强势、过度保护之嫌'，与末句 Constant health scares 呼应。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"follow up"},{"key":"B","text":"end up"},{"key":"C","text":"open up"},{"key":"D","text":"pick up"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"20.","reason":"全句作收尾，表'终将落得没人听' 线索是末句的收束语义 Constant health scares just __(20)__ with no one listening。作者讽刺'没完没了的健康恐吓最终落得没人理睬'，需表'最终沦为某种结果'的短语，end up（最终落得）+ with 正合。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"follow up'跟进、追踪'，与'落得没人听'的收尾结果义不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"end up'最终落得、以……告终'，'没完没了的健康恐吓最终落得无人理睬'，与 with no one listening 搭配自然，是作者批评 FSA 的收束之笔。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"open up'打开、开放'，与'落得没人听'语义无关。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"pick up'捡起、回升、好转'，反而是积极/上扬义，与'没人听'的消极结局相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"A group of Labour MPs, among them Yvette Cooper, are bringing in the new year with a call to institute a UK \"town of culture\" award. The proposal is that it should sit alongside the existing city of culture title, which was held by Hull in 2017, and has been awarded to Coventry for 2021. Cooper and her colleagues argue that the success of the crown for Hull, where it brought in £220m of investment and an avalanche of arts, ought not to be confined to cities. Britain's towns, it is true, are not prevented from applying, but they generally lack the resources to put together a bid to beat their bigger competitors. A town of culture award could, it is argued, become an annual event, attracting funding and creating jobs."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Some might see the proposal as a booby prize for the fact that Britain is no longer able to apply for the much more prestigious title of European capital of culture, a sought-after award bagged by Glasgow in 1990 and Liverpool in 2008. A cynic might speculate that the UK is on the verge of disappearing into an endless fever of self-celebration in its desperation to reinvent itself for the post-Brexit world: after town of culture, who knows what will follow—village of culture? Suburb of culture? Hamlet of culture?"},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"It is also wise to recall that such titles are not a cure-all. A badly run \"year of culture\" washes in and washes out of a place like the tide, bringing prominence for a spell but leaving no lasting benefits to the community. The really successful holders of such titles are those that do a great deal more than fill hotel bedrooms and bring in high-profile arts events and good press for a year. They transform the aspirations of the people who live there; they nudge the self-image of the city into a bolder and more optimistic light. It is hard to get right, and requires a remarkable degree of vision, as well as cooperation between city authorities, the private sector, community groups and cultural organisations. But it can be done: Glasgow's year as European capital of culture can certainly be seen as one of a complex series of factors that have turned the city into the powerhouse of art, music and theatre that it remains today."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"A \"town of culture\" could be not just about the arts but about honouring a town's peculiarities—helping sustain its high street, supporting local facilities and above all celebrating its people. Jeremy Wright, the culture secretary, should welcome this positive, hope-filled proposal, and turn it into action."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"Cooper and her colleagues argue that a \"town of culture\" award could____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"consolidate the town-city ties in Britain."},{"key":"B","text":"promote cooperation among Britain's towns."},{"key":"C","text":"increase the economic strength of Britain's towns."},{"key":"D","text":"focus Britain's limited resources on cultural events."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Cooper 及其同事认为\"文化城镇\"奖项可以","choicesZh":{"A":"巩固英国城镇与城市之间的联系。","B":"促进英国各城镇之间的合作。","C":"增强英国城镇的经济实力。","D":"将英国有限的资源集中用于文化活动。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Cooper and her colleagues argue that a \"town of culture\" award could____ 问的是某人具体主张了什么，对应原文一句可以坐实，属典型细节题。","parse":"题干主干为 Cooper and her colleagues argue that a \"town of culture\" award could____，that 引导宾语从句，从句主语是 a town of culture award，could 后接动词原形——四个选项都是动词短语，是 could 的补全部分。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"A town of culture award could, it is argued, become an annual event, attracting funding and creating jobs.","locateZh":"有人主张，town of culture 奖项可以成为年度活动，吸引资金、创造就业。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"consolidate the town-city ties in Britain 说\"巩固英国小镇与城市的纽带\"，文中只比较 city of culture 与 town of culture 谁更有资源，并未谈两者之间的\"纽带\"关系。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"promote cooperation among Britain's towns 说\"促进小镇之间合作\"，原文 Cooper 的论点是给单个小镇带来资金/就业，并非促成小镇间合作；only 第三段提到的 cooperation 是 city authorities/private sector/community groups/cultural organisations 之间，与 B 完全不同。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是\"带来资金和就业\"，C 把它抽象为 economic strength，且 of Britain's towns 也对应 Britain's towns，对位精准。","pairs":[{"orig":"attracting funding and creating jobs","opt":"increase the economic strength of Britain's towns"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"focus Britain's limited resources on cultural events 说\"把英国有限资源集中到文化活动上\"。原文是\"小镇 lack the resources to put together a bid\"——讲的是小镇缺乏申报资源，不是讲国家要把资源集中投向文化活动。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"According to Paragraph 2, the proposal might be regarded by some as____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a sensible compromise."},{"key":"B","text":"a self-deceiving attempt."},{"key":"C","text":"an eye-catching bonus."},{"key":"D","text":"an inaccessible target."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第二段,该提案可能被一些人视为","choicesZh":{"A":"一种明智的妥协。","B":"一次自欺欺人的尝试。","C":"一项引人注目的额外好处。","D":"一个无法实现的目标。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 the proposal might be regarded by some as____ 限定到某一段内某些人的具体评价，可在段内直接坐实。","parse":"According to Paragraph 2, the proposal might be regarded by some as____：被动语态 be regarded by some as，by 引出施动者 some，as 后接表语——四个选项都是名词短语，填入 as 之后。注意 might 是缓和语气，并非削弱归属，仍是\"some\"的看法。","locateEn":"A cynic might speculate that the UK is on the verge of disappearing into an endless fever of self-celebration in its desperation to reinvent itself for the post-Brexit world: after town of culture, who knows what will follow—village of culture? Suburb of culture? Hamlet of culture?","locateZh":"一位愤世嫉俗者也许会推测：英国正濒临陷入无休止的自我庆祝狂热，急切地想为后脱欧时代重塑自身——继 town of culture 之后，谁知道接下来会是什么？village of culture？suburb of culture？hamlet of culture？","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"a sensible compromise 说\"理性的妥协\"，sensible 是正向词；而 cynic / desperation / endless fever of self-celebration 全是贬义/嘲讽语气，谈不上 sensible。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是\"无奈处境下的自我安慰\"，a self-deceiving attempt 用 self-deceiving 一词精准对应原文 desperation + self-celebration 的复合语义。","pairs":[{"orig":"in its desperation to reinvent itself for the post-Brexit world","opt":"a self-deceiving attempt"},{"orig":"Some might see the proposal as a booby prize","opt":"a self-deceiving attempt"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"an eye-catching bonus 说\"吸睛的额外好处\"，bonus 与 eye-catching 都是正向词；原文 cynic 视角是说\"已经失去大奖，只能拿小奖自我庆祝\"，并非把它视作 bonus。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"an inaccessible target 说\"难以达成的目标\"。原文 some 的视角根本不是说提案难达成，而是说提案本身是 booby prize/自我庆祝；况且 inaccessible 的目标在原文是 European capital of culture（脱欧后申报不了），不是 town of culture 提案本身。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"The author suggests that a title holder is successful only if it____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"endeavours to maintain its image."},{"key":"B","text":"meets the aspiration of its people."},{"key":"C","text":"brings its local arts to prominence."},{"key":"D","text":"commits to its long-term growth."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者认为称号持有者只有在以下情况下才算成功","choicesZh":{"A":"努力维护其形象。","B":"满足其民众的期望。","C":"使其本地艺术声名显赫。","D":"致力于其长期发展。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The author suggests that a title holder is successful only if it____ 表面有 suggests，实质是问作者明确写出的成功条件，定位句可一句坐实，按细节题处理。","parse":"The author suggests that a title holder is successful only if it____：suggests 引导宾语从句，从句内嵌一个 only if 条件状语从句，主语 it 指代 title holder。选项是 only if 从句的谓语部分，要满足\"必要条件\"的语义。","locateEn":"The really successful holders of such titles are those that do a great deal more than fill hotel bedrooms and bring in high-profile arts events and good press for a year. They transform the aspirations of the people who live there; they nudge the self-image of the city into a bolder and more optimistic light.","locateZh":"真正成功的称号持有者，是那些做的远远不止于把酒店住满、办一年高调艺术活动、博取一年好评的城市。它们改变当地居民的志向，把城市的自我形象推向更大胆、更乐观的境界。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"endeavours to maintain its image 说\"努力维持其形象\"，但原文是 nudge the self-image into a bolder and more optimistic light——是把自我形象\"推向更大胆、更乐观\"的新境界，是改变而非维持。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"meets the aspiration of its people 说\"满足居民的志向\"，但原文是 transform the aspirations——是\"改变/重塑\"志向，不是满足现有志向。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"brings its local arts to prominence 说\"把当地艺术推向卓越\"，但原文 high-profile arts events 是被作者列为\"做得不够\"的那一类短期活动，不是\"真正成功\"的标准；prominence 一词在文中也只对应 bringing prominence for a spell（短暂关注），即被否定的现象。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是\"做超越一年的长期改造\"，D 的 long-term 精准对应 more than ... for a year 的反面，growth 是 transform aspirations / nudge self-image 的抽象上位词，对位精准。","pairs":[{"orig":"do a great deal more than fill hotel bedrooms and bring in high-profile arts events and good press for a year","opt":"commits to its long-term growth"},{"orig":"transform the aspirations of the people who live there","opt":"commits to its long-term growth"}]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"Glasgow is mentioned in Paragraph 3 to present____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a contrasting case."},{"key":"B","text":"a supporting example."},{"key":"C","text":"a background story."},{"key":"D","text":"a related topic."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"第三段提到 Glasgow 是为了呈现","choicesZh":{"A":"一个对比案例。","B":"一个支持性例证。","C":"一个背景故事。","D":"一个相关话题。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Glasgow is mentioned in Paragraph 3 to present____ 直接问举例的目的，是典型例证目的题。","parse":"Glasgow is mentioned in Paragraph 3 to present____：present 是不定式 to 的动词，宾语就是四个选项里的名词短语。要分清\"提及 Glasgow 是为了呈现什么\"——焦点在 to present 后接什么类型的论证素材。","locateEn":"But it can be done: Glasgow's year as European capital of culture can certainly be seen as one of a complex series of factors that have turned the city into the powerhouse of art, music and theatre that it remains today.","locateZh":"但这是可以做到的：Glasgow 当年作为欧洲文化之都的那一年，完全可视为一系列复杂因素之一，正是这些因素把它变成了今天依然如是的艺术、音乐、戏剧重镇。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"a contrasting case 说\"形成对比的案例\"，但 Glasgow 与前文是\"主张-佐证\"关系，不存在\"对比/反衬\"——前文没有给出一个失败案例与 Glasgow 对照。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Glasgow 是为前一句\"虽难但能做成\"的主张佐证的，正是 supporting example 的功能。","pairs":[{"orig":"But it can be done: Glasgow's year as European capital of culture can certainly be seen as one of a complex series of factors that have turned the city into the powerhouse of art, music and theatre that it remains today","opt":"a supporting example"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"a background story 说\"背景故事\"，意味着只是铺垫/背景介绍，与论点关联弱。但 Glasgow 是直接被作者用 can certainly be seen as ... 来论证 It can be done 的，是核心证据而非背景。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"a related topic 说\"相关话题\"，仅意味着\"与主话题有关联\"，没指明是支持还是反驳，把明确的支持关系模糊化了。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"What is the author's attitude towards the proposal?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Skeptical."},{"key":"B","text":"Objective."},{"key":"C","text":"Favourable."},{"key":"D","text":"Critical."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者对该提案持什么态度?","choicesZh":{"A":"怀疑的。","B":"客观的。","C":"赞成的。","D":"批判的。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What is the author's attitude towards the proposal? 含 attitude 一词，且四个选项均为态度形容词。","parse":"What is the author's attitude towards the proposal?：特殊疑问句，attitude towards X 锁定态度对象。选项均为单形容词，注意 Objective 中性、Favourable 正向，区分时要看作者是否仅\"客观陈述\"还是带有正向推动语气。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Skeptical 说\"怀疑的\"，与作者末段 should welcome / positive / hope-filled 的态度完全相反；持 Skeptical 态度的是第二段的 A cynic，作者用 might / Some 表明那只是别人的视角。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Objective 说\"客观的\"，意味着只陈述事实、不表态。但 should welcome this positive, hope-filled proposal, and turn it into action 明确表态、且带情感倾向——作者并非客观旁观者。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"末段作者用祈使式语气直接呼吁文化大臣\"应当欢迎该提案并付诸行动\"，且配以 positive / hope-filled 等正向定语——Favourable 是唯一对位项。","pairs":[{"orig":"should welcome this positive, hope-filled proposal, and turn it into action","opt":"Favourable"},{"orig":"But it can be done","opt":"Favourable"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Critical 说\"批评的\"，但作者在末段直接呼吁文化大臣\"应当欢迎并付诸行动\"，是支持而非批评；P3 中的 hard to get right 是提醒做好的难度，并非对提案本身的批评。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Scientific publishing has long been a licence to print money. Scientists need journals in which to publish their research, so they will supply the articles without monetary reward. Other scientists perform the specialised work of peer review also for free, because it is a central element in the acquisition of status and the production of scientific knowledge."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"With the content of papers secured for free, the publisher needs only find a market for its journal. Until this century, university libraries were not very price sensitive. Scientific publishers routinely report profit margins approaching 40% on their operations at a time when the rest of the publishing industry is in an existential crisis."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"The Dutch giant Elsevier, which claims to publish 25% of the scientific papers produced in the world, made profits of more than £900m last year, while UK universities alone spent more than £210m in 2016 to enable researchers to access their own publicly funded research; both figures seem to rise unstoppably despite increasingly desperate efforts to change them."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"The most drastic, and thoroughly illegal, reaction has been the emergence of Sci-Hub, a kind of global photocopier for scientific papers, set up in 2012, which now claims to offer access to every paywalled article published since 2015. The success of Sci-Hub, which relies on researchers passing on copies they have themselves legally accessed, shows the legal ecosystem has lost legitimacy among its users and must be transformed so that it works for all participants."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"In Britain the move towards open access publishing has been driven by funding bodies. In some ways it has been very successful. More than half of all British scientific research is now published under open access terms: either freely available from the moment of publication, or paywalled for a year or more so that the publishers can make a profit before being placed on general release."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"Yet the new system has not yet worked out any cheaper for the universities. Publishers have responded to the demand that they make their product free to readers by charging their writers fees to cover the costs of preparing an article. These range from around £500 to £5,000, and apparently the work gets more expensive the more that publishers do it. A report last year pointed out that the costs both of subscriptions and of these \"article preparation costs\" had been steadily rising at a rate above inflation. In some ways the scientific publishing model resembles the economy of the social internet: labour is provided free in exchange for the hope of status, while huge profits are made by a few big firms who run the market places. In both cases, we need a rebalancing of power."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"Scientific publishing is seen as \"a licence to print money\" partly because____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"its funding has enjoyed a steady increase."},{"key":"B","text":"its marketing strategy has been successful."},{"key":"C","text":"its payment for peer review is reduced."},{"key":"D","text":"its content acquisition costs nothing."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"科学出版被视为\"印钞许可证\",部分原因是____","choicesZh":{"A":"其资金获得了稳定增长。","B":"其营销策略取得了成功。","C":"其同行评审的费用降低了。","D":"其内容获取成本为零。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Scientific publishing is seen as \"a licence to print money\" partly because____ 指向原文某一条具体表述，不是要主旨、不是要态度、不是要推断，只要还原原文给出的原因。","parse":"Scientific publishing is seen as \"a licence to print money\" partly because____ 主干是被动语态 is seen as，相当于「被视作……」；partly because 引出原因状语从句的空位，正确项需是一个完整的从句内容，且只是「部分原因」之一。","locateEn":"Scientists need journals in which to publish their research, so they will supply the articles without monetary reward.","locateZh":"科学家需要期刊来发表自己的研究，所以他们会无偿提供文章。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未提及科学出版业「funding（拨款/资助）」在增加；它谈的是利润与售价。把利润误读成「资助」属典型张冠李戴。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是利润率高 profit margins approaching 40%，并未把它归因于 marketing strategy（营销策略）；高利润源于「内容免费 + 图书馆不敏感」，不是营销。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文说同行评审 also for free——是「零报酬」，不是「报酬被削减（reduced）」；reduce 隐含「原本有、现在变少」，原文从未表明评审过去拿过钱。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判「内容来源不花钱」与 its content acquisition costs nothing 是同一意思的不同说法，且题干 partly because 只要求给出一个原因——D 给出的正是定位句给出的核心原因。","pairs":[{"orig":"they will supply the articles without monetary reward","opt":"its content acquisition costs nothing"},{"orig":"Other scientists perform the specialised work of peer review also for free","opt":"its content acquisition costs nothing"}]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 2 and 3, scientific publishers Elsevier have____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"thrived mainly on university libraries."},{"key":"B","text":"gone through an existential crisis."},{"key":"C","text":"revived the publishing industry."},{"key":"D","text":"financed researchers generously."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第2段和第3段,科学出版商Elsevier____","choicesZh":{"A":"主要依靠大学图书馆而兴旺发展。","B":"经历了一场生存危机。","C":"使出版业重获生机。","D":"慷慨资助了研究人员。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 scientific publishers Elsevier have____ 是对 Elsevier 这一主体在限定段落内「做了/拥有什么」的事实性追问，落点是原文事实而非推断。","parse":"According to Paragraphs 2 and 3, scientific publishers Elsevier have____ 现在完成时 have ____ 留出谓语动词或介词短语的空位，正确项需补完一个完整谓语，描述 Elsevier 的状况或所做之事。","locateEn":"The Dutch giant Elsevier, which claims to publish 25% of the scientific papers produced in the world, made profits of more than £900m last year, while UK universities alone spent more than £210m in 2016 to enable researchers to access their own publicly funded research.","locateZh":"号称发表了全球 25% 科研论文的荷兰巨头爱思唯尔去年获利超过 9 亿英镑，而仅英国的大学就在 2016 年花了 2.1 亿多英镑，让研究者去获取他们自己用公共资金完成的研究。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Elsevier 赚 9 亿、大学花 2.1 亿——这两个数字之间的因果对照就是「Elsevier 兴旺主要靠大学图书馆」的最直接证据，A 项与预判完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"UK universities alone spent more than £210m in 2016 to enable researchers to access their own publicly funded research","opt":"thrived mainly on university libraries"},{"orig":"Until this century, university libraries were not very price sensitive","opt":"thrived mainly on university libraries"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 at a time when the rest of the publishing industry is in an existential crisis 说的是「出版业的其他部分」陷入生存危机，正是用来反衬科学出版商利润优渥；Elsevier 不仅没陷入危机，反而是反例。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文说 Elsevier 自身利润高，但从未说它「复兴了出版业」；恰恰相反，作者描绘的是其他出版业陷入危机、而科学出版商独自暴利，二者是并存而非因果。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文清楚说明 UK universities alone spent more than £210m in 2016 to enable researchers to access their own publicly funded research——是大学付钱给出版商以接触本属自己资助的研究，而非出版商「慷慨资助研究者」。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"How does the author feel about the success of Sci-Hub?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Relieved."},{"key":"B","text":"Puzzled."},{"key":"C","text":"Concerned."},{"key":"D","text":"Encouraged."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者对Sci-Hub的成功持何种态度?","choicesZh":{"A":"如释重负。","B":"困惑不解。","C":"感到担忧。","D":"深受鼓舞。"},"analysis":{"type":"How does the author feel about the success of Sci-Hub? 直接问 the author 的 feel，是典型作者态度题；不可拿 Sci-Hub 创办者或读者的态度替代。","parse":"How does the author feel about the success of Sci-Hub? 一般疑问句结构 How does X feel about Y；about 后的宾语是 the success of Sci-Hub，注意作者评价的是「Sci-Hub 的成功」这一现象，而非 Sci-Hub 本身的合法与否。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"relieved 意为「松一口气」，要求事情向好转的方向收尾；原文却说现行生态 has lost legitimacy、必须被改造——情势恶化中，谈不上 relieved。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"puzzled 意为「困惑、看不懂」，需要文本中出现「不明白/疑问」的信号；作者的论证非常明确——他知道 Sci-Hub 为何出现、并主张体系必须改变，毫无困惑可言。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"把段内 drastic / illegal / lost legitimacy / must be transformed 四处评价词合并看，作者的态度极性是负向的忧虑——对应 Concerned 是唯一与预判极性一致的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"the legal ecosystem has lost legitimacy among its users and must be transformed","opt":"Concerned"},{"orig":"The most drastic, and thoroughly illegal, reaction has been the emergence of Sci-Hub","opt":"Concerned"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"encouraged 表「受到鼓舞」，意味着作者把 Sci-Hub 视为正面榜样；但原文用 drastic, and thoroughly illegal 给它打了负标签，作者只是借其成功反推体系失效，并非为其欢呼。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"It can be learned from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that open access terms____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"allow publishers some room to make money."},{"key":"B","text":"render publishing much easier for scientists."},{"key":"C","text":"reduce the cost of publication substantially."},{"key":"D","text":"free universities from financial burdens."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第5段和第6段可以得知,开放获取条款____","choicesZh":{"A":"给出版商留有一定的盈利空间。","B":"使科学家发表论文变得更加容易。","C":"大幅降低了出版成本。","D":"使大学摆脱了经济负担。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be learned from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that open access terms____ 用 It can be learned 表「可推知」，要求一步逻辑延伸，而非原文字面复述。","parse":"It can be learned from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that open access terms____ 主句 It can be learned from… that… 是常见推断引导句；from 短语限定证据范围、that 从句承载推断对象，主语是 open access terms。","locateEn":"More than half of all British scientific research is now published under open access terms: either freely available from the moment of publication, or paywalled for a year or more so that the publishers can make a profit before being placed on general release.","locateZh":"如今英国超过一半的科研成果是按开放获取条款发表的：要么从发表那一刻起就免费可读，要么先用付费墙挡上一年以上、让出版商先赚一笔，然后再普遍开放。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判「保留盈利窗口」与 allow publishers some room to make money 的语义完全一致，且 some 这种温和限定词与原文「先一年付费墙」「转向作者收费」的现实力度相称，过强或过弱的选项都不及它。","pairs":[{"orig":"paywalled for a year or more so that the publishers can make a profit before being placed on general release","opt":"allow publishers some room to make money"},{"orig":"Publishers have responded to the demand that they make their product free to readers by charging their writers fees to cover the costs of preparing an article","opt":"allow publishers some room to make money"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文从头到尾在谈费用与利润，没有任何句子说开放获取让科学家「发表（publishing）」变得更容易；相反，科学家还要承担 fees 从 £500 to £5,000 不等，反而更难。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文明确指出 the costs both of subscriptions and of these \"article preparation costs\" had been steadily rising at a rate above inflation——成本不仅没大幅下降，反而稳步上涨且高于通胀，与 reduce substantially 完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文第 6 段开门见山：Yet the new system has not yet worked out any cheaper for the universities——开放获取尚未让大学省钱，更谈不上「让大学摆脱财务负担」。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"Which of the following characterizes the scientific publishing model?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Trial subscription is offered."},{"key":"B","text":"Labour triumphs over status."},{"key":"C","text":"Costs are well controlled."},{"key":"D","text":"The few feed on the many."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项是科学出版模式的特征?","choicesZh":{"A":"提供试用订阅。","B":"劳动胜过地位。","C":"成本得到良好控制。","D":"少数人依靠多数人为生。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following characterizes the scientific publishing model? 问的是「哪一项能概括这一模式」，答案须覆盖全文，是典型主旨题。","parse":"Which of the following characterizes the scientific publishing model? 主语是 Which of the following，谓语 characterizes 接宾语 the scientific publishing model；正确项作为主语应能合理担任「概括者」的角色。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"全文谈的是订阅费、利润、论文准备费等，未提及任何「trial subscription（试用订阅）」机制；这是一个原文完全没有出现的商业概念。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文恰好相反：劳动是为了 the hope of status 而被免费付出——status 才是劳动的回报筹码，并非「劳动战胜了地位」；将「劳动追求地位」反读为「劳动击败地位」完全颠倒原文。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 the costs both of subscriptions and of these \"article preparation costs\" had been steadily rising at a rate above inflation 明确成本上涨且超通胀，与 well controlled（被良好控制）正面冲突。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"末段类比 huge profits are made by a few big firms vs labour is provided free 与 The few feed on the many 几乎是字面对应；同时 D 覆盖了全文五个区间共同的核心结构——少数与多数之间的不对称依附。","pairs":[{"orig":"labour is provided free in exchange for the hope of status, while huge profits are made by a few big firms who run the market places","opt":"The few feed on the many"},{"orig":"they will supply the articles without monetary reward","opt":"The few feed on the many"},{"orig":"made profits of more than £900m last year","opt":"The few feed on the many"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"Progressives often support diversity mandates as a path to equality and a way to level the playing field. But all too often such policies are an insincere form of virtue-signaling that benefits only the most privileged and does little to help average people."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"A pair of bills sponsored by Massachusetts state Senator Jason Lewis and House Speaker Pro Tempore Patricia Haddad, to ensure \"gender parity\" on boards and commissions, provides a case in point."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Haddad and Lewis are concerned that more than half the state-government boards are less than 40 percent female. In order to ensure that elite women have more such opportunities, they have proposed imposing government quotas. If the bills become law, state boards and commissions will be required to set aside 50 percent of board seats for women by 2022."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"The bills are similar to a measure recently adopted in California, which last year became the first state to require gender quotas for private companies. In signing the measure, California Governor Jerry Brown admitted that the law, which expressly classifies people on the basis of sex, is probably unconstitutional."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"The US Supreme Court frowns on sex-based classifications unless they are designed to address an \"important\" policy interest. Because the California law applies to all boards, even where there is no history of prior discrimination, courts are likely to rule that the law violates the constitutional guarantee of \"equal protection\"."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-6","text":"But are such government mandates even necessary? Female participation on corporate boards may not currently mirror the percentage of women in the general population, but so what?"},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-7","text":"The number of women on corporate boards has been steadily increasing without government interference. According to a study by Catalyst, between 2010 and 2015 the share of women on the boards of global corporations increased by 54 percent."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-8","text":"Requiring companies to make gender the primary qualification for board membership will inevitably lead to less experienced private sector boards. That is exactly what happened when Norway adopted a nationwide corporate gender quota."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-9","text":"Writing in The New Republic, Alice Lee notes that increasing the number of opportunities for board membership without increasing the pool of qualified women to serve on such boards has led to a \"golden skirt\" phenomenon, where the same elite women scoop up multiple seats on a variety of boards."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-10","text":"Next time somebody pushes corporate quotas as a way to promote gender equity, remember that such policies are largely self-serving measures that make their sponsors feel good but do little to help average women."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"The author believes that the bills sponsored by Lewis and Haddad will____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"help little to reduce gender bias."},{"key":"B","text":"pose a threat to the state government."},{"key":"C","text":"raise women's position in politics."},{"key":"D","text":"greatly broaden career options."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者认为由Lewis和Haddad提案的法案将____","choicesZh":{"A":"对减少性别偏见几乎没有帮助。","B":"对州政府构成威胁。","C":"提高女性在政界的地位。","D":"极大地拓宽职业选择。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author believes that the bills sponsored by Lewis and Haddad will____ 指向某一具体对象的作者评价，答案应能在文章对该对象的评论句里直接找到对应。","parse":"The author believes that the bills sponsored by Lewis and Haddad will____ 是主句 The author believes 带 that 宾语从句，从句主语 the bills 后跟过去分词短语 sponsored by Lewis and Haddad 作后置定语，谓语 will____ 留空待选项补齐——选项是 will 后的动词原形短语。结构常规、无陷阱。","locateEn":"A pair of bills sponsored by Massachusetts state Senator Jason Lewis and House Speaker Pro Tempore Patricia Haddad, to ensure \"gender parity\" on boards and commissions, provides a case in point.","locateZh":"马萨诸塞州参议员 Jason Lewis 与众议院临时议长 Patricia Haddad 提出的两项旨在确保董事会和委员会“性别均等”的法案，就是一个典型例证。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"对消除性别不平等几乎没用\"与 help little to reduce gender bias 在否定方向（little）与施事意图（reduce bias = help average people）上完全对应，A 锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"does little to help average people","opt":"help little to reduce gender bias"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"全文论证集中在\"对普通女性无效\"与\"可能违宪\"，从未把矛头指向\"威胁州政府\"这一新主体。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"state-government boards 指州属委员会/董事会席位，属\"任职机会\"，与 raise women's position in politics（提升女性政治地位）不是一回事；且作者总评是\"无效\"，方向相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"作者通篇主张该法案 does little to help average people、do little to help average women，不会有 greatly broaden career options 的效果；且原文谈的是 board seats，不是 career options 整体。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"Which of the following is true of the California measure?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It has irritated private business owners."},{"key":"B","text":"It is welcomed by the Supreme Court."},{"key":"C","text":"It may go against the Constitution."},{"key":"D","text":"It will settle the prior controversies."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于加利福尼亚州的措施,下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"它激怒了私营企业主。","B":"它受到最高法院的欢迎。","C":"它可能违反宪法。","D":"它将解决先前的争议。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true of the California measure? 问对该法案的事实性陈述，属于典型细节题题干。","parse":"Which of the following is true of the California measure? 是 which 引导的特殊疑问句，true of the California measure 是介词短语作 true 的范围限定，结构平铺、无陷阱。","locateEn":"In signing the measure, California Governor Jerry Brown admitted that the law, which expressly classifies people on the basis of sex, is probably unconstitutional.","locateZh":"在签署该法案时，加州州长杰里·布朗承认，这部明确按性别对人进行分类的法律可能违宪。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"全文论及加州法案的部分只谈合宪性与法律分析，未涉及 private business owners 的反应。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"The US Supreme Court frowns on sex-based classifications 中 frowns on 是不悦/反对，与 welcomed by 完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"可能违宪\"与 may go against the Constitution 在情态\"可能\"与语义\"违宪\"上完全对应，C 锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"is probably unconstitutional","opt":"It may go against the Constitution"},{"orig":"the law violates the constitutional guarantee of \"equal protection\"","opt":"It may go against the Constitution"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"no history of prior discrimination 只是说\"无此前的歧视记录\"，是论证违宪的依据；从未说法案能 settle the prior controversies。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"The author mentions the study by Catalyst to illustrate____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the harm from arbitrary board decision."},{"key":"B","text":"the importance of constitutional guarantees."},{"key":"C","text":"the pressure on women in global corporations."},{"key":"D","text":"the needlessness of government interventions."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者提到Catalyst的研究是为了说明____","choicesZh":{"A":"董事会武断决策造成的危害。","B":"宪法保障的重要性。","C":"全球性公司中女性承受的压力。","D":"政府干预的不必要性。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author mentions the study by Catalyst to illustrate____ 是典型例证目的题句式，问的是\"举这个例子是为了说明什么\"。","parse":"The author mentions the study by Catalyst to illustrate____ 主谓宾结构 The author mentions the study，by Catalyst 作 study 的后置定语，to illustrate 是不定式作目的状语，____ 是 illustrate 的宾语，选项即被说明的内容。","locateEn":"The number of women on corporate boards has been steadily increasing without government interference. According to a study by Catalyst, between 2010 and 2015 the share of women on the boards of global corporations increased by 54 percent.","locateZh":"在没有政府干预的情况下，企业董事会中的女性人数一直在稳步上升。根据 Catalyst 的一项研究，2010 至 2015 年间，全球公司董事会中的女性比例增长了 54%。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"数据只显示女性董事比例增长，未涉及 arbitrary board decision（任意/武断决策）这一概念。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"宪法话题属于 P5 的论证，与 P7 的 Catalyst 例证服务的论点（无需政府干预）不在同一论证链上。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"has been steadily increasing 是中性偏正面的事实陈述，并未提及女性在跨国公司中承受何种压力。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"无需政府干预\"与 the needlessness of government interventions 在内核（不需要+政府干预）上完全一致，D 锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"without government interference","opt":"the needlessness of government interventions"},{"orig":"But are such government mandates even necessary?","opt":"the needlessness of government interventions"}]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"Norway's adoption of a nationwide corporate gender quota has led to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the underestimation of elite women's role."},{"key":"B","text":"the objection to female participation on boards."},{"key":"C","text":"the entry of unqualified candidates into the board."},{"key":"D","text":"the growing tension between labor and management."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"挪威在全国范围内采用企业性别配额已导致____","choicesZh":{"A":"对精英女性作用的低估。","B":"对女性参与董事会的反对。","C":"不合格候选人进入董事会。","D":"劳资关系日益紧张。"},"analysis":{"type":"Norway's adoption of a nationwide corporate gender quota has led to____ 问某项政策实施后导致了什么，是结果型细节题。","parse":"Norway's adoption of a nationwide corporate gender quota has led to____ 主语是 Norway's adoption（名词化结构，\"挪威采纳……一事\"），后接 of 短语作 adoption 的内容补充，谓语 has led to 后空缺由选项填——选项是一个名词短语。","locateEn":"Requiring companies to make gender the primary qualification for board membership will inevitably lead to less experienced private sector boards. That is exactly what happened when Norway adopted a nationwide corporate gender quota.","locateZh":"要求公司把性别当成进入董事会的首要资格，必然导致私营董事会经验下降。挪威在全国范围内推行公司性别配额时，发生的正是这种情况。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the same elite women scoop up multiple seats 描述精英女性\"通吃\"多席位，并非她们的角色被低估。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"全文只反对\"用配额强推\"，而非反对女性参与董事会本身；promote gender equity 仍是被作者承认的目标。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"经验/资质不足的人进入董事会\"与 the entry of unqualified candidates into the board 一一对应，C 锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"will inevitably lead to less experienced private sector boards","opt":"the entry of unqualified candidates into the board"},{"orig":"without increasing the pool of qualified women to serve on such boards","opt":"the entry of unqualified candidates into the board"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"全文论证停留在配额对董事会经验和资质的影响，从未触及 labor and management 的关系。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"Which of the following can be inferred from the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Women's need in employment should be considered."},{"key":"B","text":"Feasibility should be a prime concern in policymaking."},{"key":"C","text":"Everyone should try hard to promote social justice."},{"key":"D","text":"Major social issues should be the focus of legislation."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从文中可以推断出下列哪项?","choicesZh":{"A":"应该考虑女性在就业方面的需求。","B":"可行性应该是政策制定中的首要考虑因素。","C":"每个人都应该努力促进社会公正。","D":"重大社会问题应该成为立法的重点。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following can be inferred from the text? 是经典推断题句式。","parse":"Which of the following can be inferred from the text? which 引导特殊疑问句，can be inferred 是情态动词+被动语态，from the text 是来源状语——直白结构，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Next time somebody pushes corporate quotas as a way to promote gender equity, remember that such policies are largely self-serving measures that make their sponsors feel good but do little to help average women.","locateZh":"下次再有人把企业配额当作促进性别平等的手段来推销时，请记住：这类政策多半是自利之举，让提案者自我感觉良好，却几乎帮不到普通女性。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文反复出现 women 的董事会席位，但议题始终是\"用强制配额是否合理\"，从未提出\"应当先考虑女性的就业需求\"这一规范主张。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"立法应先考虑可行性与实效\"与 Feasibility should be a prime concern in policymaking 完全对应——主线五处证据都指向\"政策能否真起作用\"这一议题，B 锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"does little to help average people","opt":"Feasibility should be a prime concern in policymaking"},{"orig":"But are such government mandates even necessary?","opt":"Feasibility should be a prime concern in policymaking"},{"orig":"will inevitably lead to less experienced private sector boards","opt":"Feasibility should be a prime concern in policymaking"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"P10 是对立法者的提醒，不是对全社会的道德号召；且作者对\"social justice\"是否能通过此类法律实现持怀疑态度。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"作者反对的是该法案的\"无效\"，而非性别平等问题\"不够重大\"；他并未划定\"什么级别的问题才值得立法\"这一议题。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"Last Thursday, the French Senate passed a digital services tax, which would impose an entirely new tax on large multinationals that provide digital services to consumers or users in France. Digital services include everything from providing a platform for selling goods and services online to targeting advertising based on user data, and the tax applies to gross revenue from such services. Many French politicians and media outlets have referred to this as a \"GAFA tax,\" meaning that it is designed to apply primarily to companies such as Google, Apple, Facebook and Amazon—in other words, multinational tech companies based in the United States."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"The digital services tax now awaits the signature of President Emmanuel Macron, who has expressed support for the measure, and it could go into effect within the next few weeks. But it has already sparked significant controversy, with the United States trade representative opening an investigation into whether the tax discriminates against American companies, which in turn could lead to trade sanctions against France."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"The French tax is not just a unilateral move by one country in need of revenue. Instead, the digital services tax is part of a much larger trend, with countries over the past few years proposing or putting in place an alphabet soup of new international tax provisions. They have included Britain's DPT. (diverted profits tax), Australia's MAAL (multinational anti-avoidance law), and India's SEP (significant economic presence) test, to name but a few. At the same time, the European Union, Spain, Britain and several other countries have all seriously contemplated digital services taxes."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"These unilateral developments differ in their specifics, but they are all designed to tax multinationals on income and revenue that countries believe they should have a right to tax, even if international tax rules do not grant them that right. In other words, they all share a view that the international tax system has failed to keep up with the current economy."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"In response to these many unilateral measures, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD) is currently working with 131 countries to reach a consensus by the end of 2020 on an international solution. Both France and the United States are involved in the organization's work, but France's digital services tax and the American response raise questions about what the future holds for the international tax system."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"France's planned tax is a clear warning: Unless a broad consensus can be reached on reforming the international tax system, other nations are likely to follow suit, and American companies will face a cascade of different taxes from dozens of nations that will prove burdensome and costly."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"The French Senate has passed a bill to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"regulate digital services platforms."},{"key":"B","text":"protect French companies' interests."},{"key":"C","text":"impose a levy on tech multinationals."},{"key":"D","text":"curb the influence of advertising."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"法国参议院已通过一项法案，旨在____","choicesZh":{"A":"监管数字服务平台。","B":"保护法国企业的利益。","C":"对科技跨国公司征税。","D":"遏制广告的影响力。"},"analysis":{"type":"The French Senate has passed a bill to____ 问的是该法案的目的，是对原文一处具体事实的客观转述。","parse":"题干 The French Senate has passed a bill to____ 为待补全陈述句，主干 The French Senate has passed a bill，不定式 to 引出待补全的目的状语，结构平铺直叙、无陷阱。","locateEn":"Last Thursday, the French Senate passed a digital services tax, which would impose an entirely new tax on large multinationals that provide digital services to consumers or users in France.","locateZh":"上周四，法国参议院通过了一项数字服务税法案，该税将对在法国为消费者或用户提供数字服务的大型跨国公司征收一项全新税种。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"regulate digital services platforms 把法案性质从「税」变成了「监管」，但原文 digital services tax 是税不是监管。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"protect French companies' interests 全文未提；原文重点是向跨国巨头征税以为本国财政增收，不是保护法企。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判「对大型跨国数字公司征新税」与 impose a levy on tech multinationals 完全等义，无添加无削减，锁定 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"impose an entirely new tax on large multinationals that provide digital services","opt":"impose a levy on tech multinationals"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"curb the influence of advertising 抓住了原文 targeting advertising based on user data 中的 advertising 一词，但原文中广告只是数字服务的一个举例，并非法案要遏制的对象。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"It can be learned from Paragraph 2 that the digital services tax____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"may trigger countermeasures against France."},{"key":"B","text":"is apt to arouse criticism at home and abroad."},{"key":"C","text":"aims to ease international trade tensions."},{"key":"D","text":"will prompt the tech giants to quit France."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第2段可以得知,数字服务税____","choicesZh":{"A":"可能会引发针对法国的反制措施。","B":"容易在国内外引起批评。","C":"旨在缓解国际贸易紧张局势。","D":"将促使科技巨头退出法国。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be learned from Paragraph 2 that… 中的 can be learned 提示答案非原文直陈，需在原文事实上做一步逻辑延伸。","parse":"题干 It can be learned from Paragraph 2 that the digital services tax____ 为 It 形式主语句，that 引导宾语从句即待补全部分；主从句结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"But it has already sparked significant controversy, with the United States trade representative opening an investigation into whether the tax discriminates against American companies, which in turn could lead to trade sanctions against France.","locateZh":"但它已引发巨大争议，美国贸易代表已就该税是否歧视美国公司展开调查，而这反过来可能导致对法国实施贸易制裁。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判「可能招致针对法国的反制」与 may trigger countermeasures against France 完全等义，且推断只走了一步，未越界。","pairs":[{"orig":"could lead to trade sanctions against France","opt":"may trigger countermeasures against France"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只提到美国一方的调查与可能制裁，未提「国内」批评；at home and abroad 把批评来源扩到「国内外」，超出原文。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文是「引发争议、可能招致制裁」，选项却说「旨在缓和国际贸易紧张」，方向完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文未提任何科技巨头会「撤出法国」之事，will prompt the tech giants to quit France 属过度推断。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"The countries adopting the unilateral measures share the opinion that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"redistribution of tech giants' revenue must be ensured."},{"key":"B","text":"the current international tax system needs upgrading."},{"key":"C","text":"tech multinationals' monopoly should be prevented."},{"key":"D","text":"all countries ought to enjoy equal taxing rights."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"采取单边措施的国家有一个共同观点,即____","choicesZh":{"A":"必须确保科技巨头收入的再分配。","B":"当前的国际税收体系需要升级。","C":"应当防止科技跨国公司的垄断。","D":"所有国家都应享有平等的征税权。"},"analysis":{"type":"Q38 问这些国家「share the opinion that…」，对应原文一处明确的共同观点陈述，是事实转述。","parse":"题干 The countries adopting the unilateral measures share the opinion that____ 中 adopting the unilateral measures 是现在分词短语作 countries 的后置定语；share the opinion that 引出宾语从句。结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"In other words, they all share a view that the international tax system has failed to keep up with the current economy.","locateZh":"换句话说，它们都持有同一种观点：国际税收体系已经跟不上当下经济。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说要对跨国巨头征税，并未涉及把税收再分配给谁。redistribution of tech giants' revenue 属原文未提之事。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判「现行国际税制已落后于经济」与 the current international tax system needs upgrading 在事实层面完全等义，B 锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"the international tax system has failed to keep up with the current economy","opt":"the current international tax system needs upgrading"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文目的是征税，与 tech multinationals' monopoly should be prevented 所说的反垄断不是一回事；垄断话题原文未提。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文说这些国家在 unilateral 地为自己争取「应有的征税权」，并不主张所有国家享有「平等征税权」；范围被悄悄扩到「all countries」。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"It can be learned from Paragraph 5 that the OECD's current work____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is being resisted by US companies."},{"key":"B","text":"needs to be readjusted immediately."},{"key":"C","text":"is faced with uncertain prospects."},{"key":"D","text":"needs to involve more countries."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第5段可以得知,OECD目前的工作____","choicesZh":{"A":"正遭到美国企业的抵制。","B":"需要立即进行调整。","C":"面临不确定的前景。","D":"需要更多国家参与。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be learned from Paragraph 5 that… 同样含 can be learned，要在原文事实上做一步外推。","parse":"题干 It can be learned from Paragraph 5 that the OECD's current work____ 与 Q37 结构同型，It 作形式主语、that 引宾从；主语是带所有格定语的 the OECD's current work，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Both France and the United States are involved in the organization's work, but France's digital services tax and the American response raise questions about what the future holds for the international tax system.","locateZh":"法国和美国都参与该组织的工作，但法国的数字服务税与美方的回应让人对国际税收体系的未来产生疑问。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文是美国贸易代表展开调查，不是 US companies 自己在抵制；行为主体也被偷换。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说前景不确定，未要求 OECD 的工作 needs to be readjusted immediately；强情态 + immediately 双重强化，是过度推断。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判「前景充满不确定性」与 is faced with uncertain prospects 在状态描述上等值，C 锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"raise questions about what the future holds for the international tax system","opt":"is faced with uncertain prospects"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文已明确 OECD 正与 131 国合作，未提需 involve more countries；选项添加了原文未有的诉求。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"Which of the following might be the best title for this text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"France Is Confronted with Trade Sanctions"},{"key":"B","text":"France leads the charge on Digital Tax"},{"key":"C","text":"France Says \"NO\" to Tech Multinationals"},{"key":"D","text":"France Demands a Role in the Digital Economy"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项最适合作为本文的标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"法国面临贸易制裁","B":"法国在数字税方面率先出击","C":"法国对科技跨国公司说\"不\"","D":"法国要求在数字经济中发挥作用"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following might be the best title for this text? 以 best title 直接挑明全文主旨题身份。","parse":"题干 Which of the following might be the best title for this text? 为 which 引导的特殊疑问句，might 缓和语气，结构简明无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"France Is Confronted with Trade Sanctions 只覆盖 P2 中「可能招致贸易制裁」一处信息，未覆盖 P3 P4 P6 的国际趋势主线。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"France leads the charge on Digital Tax 一句话概括了「法国率先 + 他国跟进」的双向逻辑，覆盖首段事件与末段预言，符合主旨题标准。","pairs":[{"orig":"the French Senate passed a digital services tax","opt":"France leads the charge on Digital Tax"},{"orig":"other nations are likely to follow suit","opt":"France leads the charge on Digital Tax"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未让法国 Says \"NO\" to Tech Multinationals，征税不等于拒绝；这些公司仍在法国正常运营，只是要交税。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"France Demands a Role in the Digital Economy 把主旨偷换为「法国要在数字经济中谋一席之地」；原文谈的是「数字税」而非「在数字经济中谋职位」。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"heading","title":"Section II Part B 小标题匹配","directions":"Directions: Read the following text and answer the questions by choosing the most suitable subheading from the list A-G for each of the numbered paragraphs (41-45). There are two extra subheadings. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"","text":"In a social situation, eye contact with another person can show that you are paying attention in a friendly way. But it can also be antagonistic, such as when a political candidate turns toward their competitor during a debate and makes eye contact that signals hostility. Here's what hard science reveals about eye contact:"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"","text":"{{41}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"","text":"We know that a typical infant will instinctively gaze into its mother's eyes, and she will look back. This mutual gaze is a major part of the attachment between mother and child. In adulthood, looking someone else in a pleasant way can be a complimentary sign of paying attention. It can catch someone's attention in a crowded room, \"Eye contact and smile\" can signal availability and confidence, a common-sense notion supported in studies by psychologist Monica Moore."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"","text":"{{42}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"","text":"Neuroscientist Bonnie Auyeung found that the hormone oxytocin increased the amount of eye contact from men toward the interviewer during a brief interview when the direction of their gaze was recorded. This was also found in high-functioning men with some autistic spectrum symptoms, who may tend to avoid eye contact. Specific brain regions that respond during direct gaze are being explored by other researchers, using advanced methods of brain scanning."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"","text":"{{43}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"","text":"With the use of eye-tracking technology, Julia Minson of the Harvard Kennedy School of Government concluded that eye contact can signal very different kinds of messages, depending on the situation. While eye contact may be a sign of connection or trust in friendly situations, it's more likely to be associated with dominance or intimidation in adversarial situations. \"Whether you're a politician or a parent, it might be helpful to keep in mind that trying to maintain eye contact may backfire if you're trying to convince someone who has a different set of beliefs than you,\" said Minson."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-8","label":"","text":"{{44}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-9","label":"","text":"When we look at a face or a picture, our eyes pause on one spot at a time, often on the eyes or mouth. These pauses typically occur at about three per second, and the eyes then jump to another spot, until several important points in the image are registered like a series of snapshots. How the whole image is then assembled and perceived is still a mystery although it is the subject of current research."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-10","label":"","text":"{{45}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-11","label":"","text":"In people who score high in a test of neuroticism, a personality dimension associated with self-consciousness and anxiety, eye contact triggered more activity associated with avoidance, according to the Finnish researcher Jari Hietanen and colleagues. \"Our findings indicate that people do not only feel different when they are the centre of attention but that their brain reactions also differ.\" A more direct finding is that people who scored highly for negative emotions like anxiety looked at others for shorter periods of time and reported more comfortable feelings when others did not look directly at them."}]},"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Eye fixations are brief"},{"key":"B","text":"Too much eye contact is instinctively felt to be rude"},{"key":"C","text":"Eye contact can be a friendly social signal"},{"key":"D","text":"Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact"},{"key":"E","text":"Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated"},{"key":"F","text":"Most people are not comfortable holding eye contact with strangers"},{"key":"G","text":"Eye contact can be aggressive."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Eye fixations are brief"},{"key":"B","text":"Too much eye contact is instinctively felt to be rude"},{"key":"C","text":"Eye contact can be a friendly social signal"},{"key":"D","text":"Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact"},{"key":"E","text":"Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated"},{"key":"F","text":"Most people are not comfortable holding eye contact with strangers"},{"key":"G","text":"Eye contact can be aggressive."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"通篇归纳","stemZh":"41. (41)____","reason":"Eye contact can be a friendly social signal 眼神接触可以是一种友好的社交信号\n眼神是传递友好、注意的善意社交信号 本段从婴儿与母亲的对视讲起，落到成年后的社交：looking someone else in a pleasant way can be a complimentary sign of paying attention，还能 catch someone's attention in a crowded room，并 signal availability and confidence。母婴对视、人群中吸引注意都是\"例子/论据\"，它们共同支撑的主旨是：目光接触是一种友好、积极的社交信号。注意 pleasant、complimentary、confidence 都是正面色彩词。\nfriendly social signal 同义对上 pleasant/complimentary Eye contact can be a friendly social signal 是本段主旨的同义改写：friendly 正对应 looking someone else in a pleasant way 的 pleasant，social signal 正对应 a complimentary sign of paying attention 与 signal availability and confidence——眼神\"发出友好的社交信号\"覆盖了全段所有正面例子，概括到位、不偏窄。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Eye contact can be a friendly social signal","clues":[]}},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Eye fixations are brief"},{"key":"B","text":"Too much eye contact is instinctively felt to be rude"},{"key":"C","text":"Eye contact can be a friendly social signal"},{"key":"D","text":"Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact"},{"key":"E","text":"Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated"},{"key":"F","text":"Most people are not comfortable holding eye contact with strangers"},{"key":"G","text":"Eye contact can be aggressive."}],"answer":"E","explanation":{"answer":"E","type":"通篇归纳","stemZh":"42. (42)____","reason":"Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated 眼神接触背后的生物学因素正在被研究\n科学家在探查眼神背后的激素与脑区机制 本段全是生理层面的研究：神经科学家发现激素催产素会增加男性的目光接触——the hormone oxytocin increased the amount of eye contact；并提到 Specific brain regions that respond during direct gaze are being explored by other researchers, using advanced methods of brain scanning。激素、脑区、脑扫描这些都是\"生物学机制\"，且都用\"正在被探索/研究\"的进行态，主旨即：眼神接触的生理基础正在被研究。\nbiological factors 同义统摄激素+脑区 Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated 是本段主旨的同义改写：biological factors 同时统摄了 the hormone oxytocin（激素）与 Specific brain regions（脑区）这两类生理因素，being investigated 正对应 are being explored by other researchers 的\"正在被研究\"。它概括的是全段而非某一项，层级恰好。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated","clues":[]}},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Eye fixations are brief"},{"key":"B","text":"Too much eye contact is instinctively felt to be rude"},{"key":"C","text":"Eye contact can be a friendly social signal"},{"key":"D","text":"Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact"},{"key":"E","text":"Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated"},{"key":"F","text":"Most people are not comfortable holding eye contact with strangers"},{"key":"G","text":"Eye contact can be aggressive."}],"answer":"G","explanation":{"answer":"G","type":"通篇归纳","stemZh":"43. (43)____","reason":"Eye contact can be aggressive. 眼神接触可能具有攻击性\n敌对情境下眼神表达支配与威胁 本段借 Minson 的眼动研究指出眼神含义因情境而异，重点落在对抗一面：it's more likely to be associated with dominance or intimidation in adversarial situations，并以 trying to maintain eye contact may backfire if you're trying to convince someone who has a different set of beliefs than you 收尾。friendly situations 只是用来作对比的铺垫，本段真正强调的是 adversarial（敌对）情境下眼神的 dominance、intimidation（支配、威胁）。\naggressive 同义概括 dominance/intimidation Eye contact can be aggressive. 是本段被强调一极的同义改写：aggressive（攻击性）正概括了 dominance or intimidation in adversarial situations 的支配、威胁与敌对，也呼应了 may backfire 的反作用。它抓的是本段真正落点，不是陪衬的 friendly 那半。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Eye contact can be aggressive.","clues":[]}},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Eye fixations are brief"},{"key":"B","text":"Too much eye contact is instinctively felt to be rude"},{"key":"C","text":"Eye contact can be a friendly social signal"},{"key":"D","text":"Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact"},{"key":"E","text":"Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated"},{"key":"F","text":"Most people are not comfortable holding eye contact with strangers"},{"key":"G","text":"Eye contact can be aggressive."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"段首","stemZh":"44. (44)____","reason":"Eye fixations are brief 眼神注视是短暂的\n看脸时眼睛一次只短暂停留一点 本段主旨句在段首：When we look at a face or a picture, our eyes pause on one spot at a time（此处指第 5 段段首，引文逐字取自该段）。接着说 These pauses typically occur at about three per second, and the eyes then jump to another spot。每秒约三次、看完就跳走，讲的全是\"注视停留一次只在一处、且很短暂\"这一眼动机制，整段是对该机制的描述。\nfixations are brief 同义对上 pause...three per second Eye fixations are brief 是本段主旨的同义改写：fixations（注视）对应 our eyes pause on one spot at a time 的 pause，brief（短暂）对应 These pauses typically occur at about three per second 与随即 jump to another spot——每秒三次、停一下就跳，正是\"注视短暂\"。整段都在说这件事，概括精准。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Eye fixations are brief","clues":[]}},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Eye fixations are brief"},{"key":"B","text":"Too much eye contact is instinctively felt to be rude"},{"key":"C","text":"Eye contact can be a friendly social signal"},{"key":"D","text":"Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact"},{"key":"E","text":"Biological factors behind eye contact are being investigated"},{"key":"F","text":"Most people are not comfortable holding eye contact with strangers"},{"key":"G","text":"Eye contact can be aggressive."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"通篇归纳","stemZh":"45. (45)____","reason":"Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact 性格会影响一个人对眼神接触的反应\n高神经质者对被注视更回避、更不适 本段把人格特质与对眼神的反应挂钩：神经质（焦虑、自我意识强）得分高的人，eye contact triggered more activity associated with avoidance；得分高于负面情绪的人 looked at others for shorter periods of time and reported more comfortable feelings when others did not look directly at them。研究者还指出 their brain reactions also differ。主旨即：人格特质不同，对目光接触的反应（回避、不适）也不同。\npersonality affects reaction 正概括人格→反应 Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact 是本段主旨的同义改写：personality 对应 a personality dimension associated with self-consciousness and anxiety（神经质这一人格维度），affect how a person reacts 对应 eye contact triggered more activity associated with avoidance 与 their brain reactions also differ——人格不同、对眼神的反应就不同，正是全段所讲。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Personality can affect how a person reacts to eye contact","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"Following the explosion of creativity in Florence during the 14th century known as the Renaissance, the modern world saw a departure from what it had once known. It turned from God and the authority of the Roman Catholic Church and instead favoured a more humanistic approach to being. Renaissance ideas had spread throughout Europe well into the 17th century, with the arts and sciences flourishing extraordinarily among those with a more logical disposition. (46) with the Church's teachings and ways of thinking eclipsed by the Renaissance, the gap between the Medieval and modern periods had been bridged leading to new and unexplored intellectual territories."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"During the Renaissance, the great minds of Nicolaus Copernicus, Johannes Kepler and Galileo Galilei demonstrated the power of scientific study and discovery. (47) Before each of their revelations, many thinkers at the time had sustained more ancient ways of thinking, including the geocentric view that the Earth was at the centre of our universe. Copernicus theorized in 1543 that all of the planets that we knew of revolved not around the Earth, but the Sun, a system that was later upheld by Galileo at his own expense. Offering up such a theory during a time of high tension between scientific and religious minds was branded as heresy and any such heretics that continued to spread these lies were to be punished by imprisonment or even death."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"(48) Despite attempts by the Church to suppress this new generation of logicians and rationalists, more explanations for how the universe functioned were being made at a rate that the people could no longer ignore. It was with these great revelations that a new kind of philosophy founded in reason was born."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-4","text":"The Church's long-standing dogma was losing the great battle for truth to rationalists and scientists. This very fact embodied the new ways of thinking that swept through Europe during most of the 17th century. (49) As many took on the duty of trying to integrate reasoning and scientific philosophies into the world, the Renaissance was over and it was time for a new era—the Age of Reason."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-5","text":"The 17th and 18th centuries were times of radical change and curiosity. Scientific method, reductionism and the questioning of Church ideals was to be encouraged, as were ideas of liberty, tolerance and progress. (50) Such actions to seek knowledge and to understand what information we already knew were captured by the Latin phrase 'sapere aude' or 'dare to know', after Immanuel Kant used it in his essay \"An Answer to the Question: What is Enlightenment?\" It was the purpose and responsibility of great minds to go forth and seek out the truth, which they believed to be founded in knowledge."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"with the Church's teachings and ways of thinking eclipsed by the Renaissance, the gap between the Medieval and modern periods had been bridged leading to new and unexplored intellectual territories.","refZh":"随着教会的教义与思维方式被文艺复兴所遮蔽，中世纪与现代之间的鸿沟得以弥合，从而通向崭新而未经探索的知识领域。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"with the Church's teachings and ways of thinking eclipsed by the Renaissance,","lit":"随着教会的教义与思维方式被文艺复兴所遮蔽，","role":"（with 引导的独立主格作状语）","note":"难点： eclipse 熟词僻义＋with 状语结构 eclipse 名词义是『日/月食』，此处作动词是僻义『使黯然失色、遮蔽、盖过』，结合主旨 It turned from God and the authority of the Roman Catholic Church 应取『被遮蔽/被盖过/黯然失色』。整块是 with + 名词 + 过去分词 的独立主格，表伴随背景，译成『随着……被……』即可。"},{"en":"the gap between the Medieval and modern periods had been bridged","lit":"中世纪与现代之间的鸿沟已被弥合","role":"（主句（被动））","note":"难点： bridge 名→动＋被动汉化 bridge 此处是动词『弥合、架起桥梁、衔接』，had been bridged 是过去完成被动。被动直译『被弥合』略生硬，可保留『被弥合』或转无主句『弥合了……鸿沟』。Medieval 译『中世纪』，与 modern『现代』对照。"},{"en":"leading to new and unexplored intellectual territories.","lit":"通向崭新而未经探索的知识领域。","role":"（现在分词作结果状语）","note":"难点： intellectual territories 抽象名词具体化 lead to 『导向、通往』；territories 本义『领土』，与 intellectual 搭配是比喻义『（知识/智识的）领域、疆域』。unexplored『未被探索的』。整块译『从而通向崭新而未经探索的知识/思想领域』，把抽象的『智识疆域』具体化为『知识领域』更通顺。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"Before each of their revelations, many thinkers at the time had sustained more ancient ways of thinking, including the geocentric view that the Earth was at the centre of our universe.","refZh":"在哥白尼等人各自做出这些发现之前，当时许多思想家一直沿袭着更为古老的思维方式，其中就包括认为地球处于宇宙中心的地心说观点。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Before each of their revelations,","lit":"在他们各自的发现/揭示之前，","role":"（时间状语）","note":"难点： their 跨句回指＋revelation 取义 their 句内无先行词，须回上句还原：指 Nicolaus Copernicus, Johannes Kepler and Galileo Galilei 这三位。revelation 本义带宗教色彩『启示』，此处语境是科学发现，取『发现/揭示/重大发现』。译时可点明为『在哥白尼等人各自做出这些发现之前』，把 their 还原。"},{"en":"many thinkers at the time had sustained more ancient ways of thinking,","lit":"当时许多思想家一直沿袭着更为古老的思维方式，","role":"（主句（过去完成））","note":"难点： sustain 熟词僻义 sustain 常见义『维持、支撑、遭受』，此处宾语是 ways of thinking，取『坚持、沿袭、保持』。had sustained 过去完成表『此前一直……』。more ancient『更古老的』，more 是比较级修饰，译『更为古老』。"},{"en":"including the geocentric view that the Earth was at the centre of our universe.","lit":"包括地球处于宇宙中心的地心说观点。","role":"（including 介词短语＋that 同位语从句）","note":"难点： geocentric 术语＋that 同位语从句 geocentric view『地心说/地心观』（geo-地+centric 中心）。关键：that the Earth was at the centre... 不是定语从句，而是 view 的同位语从句（that 后是完整句、解释 view 的内容），译成『……这一观点』，把 that 从句内容前置到 view 之前作其内容。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"Despite attempts by the Church to suppress this new generation of logicians and rationalists, more explanations for how the universe functioned were being made at a rate that the people could no longer ignore.","refZh":"尽管教会试图压制这一代新兴的逻辑学家和理性主义者，但关于宇宙如何运行的解释仍被不断提出，其势头之快，人们再也无法忽视。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Despite attempts by the Church to suppress this new generation of logicians and rationalists,","lit":"尽管教会试图压制这一代新兴的逻辑学家和理性主义者，","role":"（Despite 引导的让步状语）","note":"难点： Despite 让步＋this 跨句回指＋名词化 attempts Despite『尽管』引导让步。attempts...to suppress 是名词化结构，译时还原成动作『试图压制』更顺。this new generation 的 this 承上文，指第2、3段被教会迫害的那批科学家/理性思考者，落实为『这一代新兴的……』即可。logicians 逻辑学家、rationalists 理性主义者。"},{"en":"more explanations for how the universe functioned were being made","lit":"越来越多关于宇宙如何运行的解释正被不断提出，","role":"（主句（过去进行被动））","note":"难点： were being made 进行被动＋how 从句作定语 were being made 是过去进行被动『正在被做出/提出』，译时宜转主动或无主句『（人们）不断提出』。for how the universe functioned 是介词 for + how 引导的名词性从句，作 explanations 的定语，译『关于宇宙如何运行的（解释）』前置。function 此处是动词『运行、运转』。"},{"en":"at a rate that the people could no longer ignore.","lit":"其速度之快是人们再也无法忽视的。","role":"（方式状语＋that 定语从句）","note":"难点： at a rate that... 定语从句＋程度含义 at a rate『以一种……的速度/势头』，that 引导定语从句修饰 rate（that 后 ignore 缺宾语，故为定语从句）。直译『以一种人们无法再忽视的速度』偏翻译腔，可拆译为『其势头/速度之快，人们再也无法忽视』，把后置定语转成一个小分句。no longer『不再、再也不』。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"As many took on the duty of trying to integrate reasoning and scientific philosophies into the world, the Renaissance was over and it was time for a new era—the Age of Reason.","refZh":"随着许多人担起将理性与科学哲学融入世界的责任，文艺复兴宣告结束，一个新时代到来了——这就是理性时代。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"As many took on the duty of trying to integrate reasoning and scientific philosophies into the world,","lit":"随着许多人担起将理性与科学哲学融入世界的责任，","role":"（As 引导的时间/原因状语从句）","note":"难点： As 多义＋many 名词性＋take on/integrate 搭配 As 此处取『随着、当……时』（表伴随/时间），不是『因为』也不是『像』。many 单独作主语＝『许多人』（承上文那批理性思考者）。take on the duty『承担/担起责任』，integrate A into B『把 A 融入 B』。reasoning 译『推理/理性思维』，与全文 reason 术语呼应。"},{"en":"the Renaissance was over","lit":"文艺复兴结束了，","role":"（并列主句一）","note":"难点： be over 短语 be over『结束、终结』，是固定搭配而非『在……上方』。Renaissance 与全文统一译『文艺复兴』。此块直白，仅提示别把 over 当方位词。"},{"en":"and it was time for a new era—the Age of Reason.","lit":"新时代到来了——理性时代。","role":"（并列主句二＋破折号同位）","note":"难点： it was time for 句型＋破折号同位语 it was time for...『是……的时候了/……到来了』，it 是形式主语，不必译出。破折号后 the Age of Reason 是 a new era 的同位语（破折号常引出解释/同位），译时保留破折号或用『即』：『一个新时代——理性时代』。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"Such actions to seek knowledge and to understand what information we already knew were captured by the Latin phrase 'sapere aude' or 'dare to know',","refZh":"这些寻求知识、理解我们已经掌握的信息的行动，被拉丁语短语 'sapere aude'（即 'dare to know'，意为『敢于求知』）所概括，","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Such actions to seek knowledge and to understand what information we already knew","lit":"这些寻求知识、理解我们已知信息的行动","role":"（主语（含两个 to do 定语＋what 宾语从句））","note":"难点： such 回指＋两个 to do 作定语＋what 从句 Such actions 的 such 承上文，指 Scientific method, reductionism and the questioning of Church ideals was to be encouraged 等求知行为，译『这类/这些行动』即可。两个 to seek...和 to understand...是并列不定式作 actions 的定语，前置译『寻求知识、理解……的（行动）』。what information we already knew 是 understand 的宾语从句『我们已经知道的信息』。"},{"en":"were captured by the Latin phrase 'sapere aude' or 'dare to know',","lit":"被拉丁语短语 'sapere aude' 即 'dare to know'（敢于求知）所概括，","role":"（谓语（被动）＋by 短语）","note":"难点： capture 熟词僻义＋被动＋or 表同义 capture 常见义『捕获、俘虏』，此处主语是抽象的 actions、宾语是 phrase，取僻义『概括、凝练、表达』——『被……短语所概括/凝练』。were captured by 被动可转主动『……短语概括了这些行动』。or 在此非『或者』，而是引出对拉丁文的英文释义『即/也就是』，dare to know＝『敢于求知/敢于认知』。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: The Students Union of your university has assigned you to inform the international students about an upcoming singing contest. White a notice in about 100 words. Write your answer on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not use your own name in the notice. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: The Students Union of your university has assigned you to inform the international students about an upcoming singing contest. White a notice in about 100 words. Write your answer on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not use your own name in the notice. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Notice To enrich campus life and celebrate cultural diversity, the Students Union is delighted to announce a singing contest specially for international students on our campus. The contest will be held in the Main Auditorium at 7 p.m. on December 15th. Participants may perform any song they love, but the piece should fit the theme \"Voices Across Cultures.\" Those interested are welcome to sign up by emailing your name and song title to su@campus.edu before December 10th. For more details, please contact Ms. Li at 123-4567. We warmly invite all international students to take part and share your wonderful voices with us! Students Union December 1st","translation":"通知\n为丰富校园生活、彰显文化多元，学生会很高兴地宣布：将专为本校国际学生举办一场歌唱比赛。\n比赛将于 12 月 15 日晚 7 点在大礼堂举行。参赛者可演唱任意自己喜爱的歌曲，但曲目应契合\"跨越文化之声\"这一主题。\n有意者欢迎于 12 月 10 日前，将姓名与曲目发送至 su@campus.edu 报名。如需了解更多详情，请致电 123-4567 联系李老师。\n我们诚挚邀请所有国际学生踊跃参加，与我们分享你动人的歌声！\n学生会 12 月 1 日","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"标题就位","text":"【第 1 段】 标题就位 。首行 Notice 单独居中，落实\"标题定文体身份\"——一眼定为通知，先稳住格式分。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"开门宣布","text":"【第 2 段】 开门宣布 。the Students Union is delighted to announce a singing contest specially for international students 用机构宣布句一句点明发布目的、亮明身份与读者，落实\"开头一句点目的\"。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"信息分条","text":"【第 3 段】 信息分条 。先 will be held in the Main Auditorium at 7 p.m. on December 15th 给全时间地点，再 the piece should fit the theme \"Voices Across Cultures.\" 给主题要求，落实\"when-where-what分条写\"。"},{"tag":"【第 4 段】","core":"报名可执行","text":"【第 4 段】 报名可执行 。sign up by emailing ... before December 10th 给报名方式与截止，contact Ms. Li at 123-4567 给联系人，落实\"报名截止联系人一条不漏\"，让通知真能被执行。"},{"tag":"【第 5 段】","core":"邀请收尾","text":"【第 5 段】 邀请收尾 。We warmly invite all international students to take part 用邀请句热情收束，落实\"结尾发出邀请\"，补全题目要求的邀请要点。"},{"tag":"【第 6 段】","core":"机构落款","text":"【第 6 段】 机构落款 。末尾 Students Union 与日期落款，全篇无真名，落实\"机构落款不署真名\"，守住题目最硬的禁令。"}],"wordCount":106}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the picture below. In your essay, you should 1)describe the picture briefly, 2)interpret the implied meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the picture below. In your essay, you should 1)describe the picture briefly, 2)interpret the implied meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2020-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅标题为“习惯”的漫画，由左右两个部分组成","width":"621","height":"518","local":"assets/writing/2020-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is depicted in the drawing entitled \"Habit\", two contrasting figures are presented. On the left, a woman sits at a desk piled with documents, bending over her work, with a bubble above her reading that she feels at ease only when tasks are finished early. On the right, a man leans back in his chair with only a book and a pen before him, looking relaxed, saying that he never starts until the last moment. Simple as it seems, the picture conveys a thought-provoking message about the power of habits. The two attitudes stand for two life styles: one embraces planning ahead and finishing early, while the other keeps putting things off until deadlines loom. What the cartoonist intends to highlight is that a good habit of getting things done in advance keeps us calm and efficient, whereas procrastination leaves us anxious and passive when time runs out. In my view, we should cultivate the good habit of acting early rather than delaying. Therefore, it is advisable to make a plan and start at once. Only in this way can we stay in control of our time and lead a more productive life.","translation":"如画中题为「习惯」的漫画所示，画面呈现出两个形成对比的人物。左侧，一位女性坐在堆满文件的办公桌前，低头伏案，她上方的对话框写着：只有尽早完成任务，她才感到安心。右侧，一位男性靠在椅背上，桌上只有一本书和一支笔，看上去很放松，他说自己不到最后一刻绝不动手。\n看似简单，这幅漫画却传达出一个发人深省的信息，关乎习惯的力量。两种态度代表两种生活方式：一种崇尚提前规划、尽早完成，另一种则一拖再拖，直到期限逼近。画家意在强调：提前把事情做完的好习惯让我们从容而高效，而拖延则让我们在时间耗尽时焦虑又被动。\n在我看来，我们应当培养尽早行动而非拖延的好习惯。因此，明智之举是制定计划、立即着手。唯有如此，我们才能掌控自己的时间，过上更高效的生活。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"客观分述左右","text":"【第 1 段】 客观分述左右 。本段用「As is depicted ... two contrasting figures are presented」总起点出对比，再以 On the left / On the right 分述两人动作，并把对话框转为间接引语（reading that ... / saying that ...），全用现在时客观陈述，落实描述段功能，对应 describe the picture briefly。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"抽象出寓意","text":"【第 2 段】 抽象出寓意 。本段以「Simple as it seems, the picture conveys a ... message」把镜头从画面拉向道理，用「The two attitudes stand for two life styles」把人物抽象成两类，再以「What the cartoonist intends to highlight is that ...」点明习惯决定状态，是采分核心，对应 interpret the implied meaning。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"表态并给建议","text":"【第 3 段】 表态并给建议 。本段以「In my view, we should ... rather than ...」亮明支持早做，用「Therefore, it is advisable to ...」给出制定计划、立刻着手的建议，末句「Only in this way can we ...」倒装拔高收尾并回扣寓意，对应 give your comments。"}],"wordCount":194}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 B On · 2 A match · 3 D enjoyment · 4 B guaranteed · 5 C issued · 6 D at · 7 B avoid · 8 C partially · 9 C While · 10 A conclusive · 11 A likely · 12 C On the basis of · 13 D advisable · 14 B After all · 15 A connection · 16 D served · 17 C To be fair · 18 A entirely · 19 D campaign · 20 B end up \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 C · 22 B · 23 D · 24 B · 25 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 D · 27 A · 28 C · 29 A · 30 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 A · 32 C · 33 D · 34 C · 35 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 C · 37 A · 38 B · 39 C · 40 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"段落小标题（7选5） Section II Part B （41–45 题） 41 C · 42 E · 43 G · 44 A · 45 D \n（逐题解析见 段落小标题（7选5）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":45,"missingSections":[]}};
